# Custom DNS records for the simulated internet.
#
# Every /etc/topgen/dns.d/*.hosts file is read when the simulation starts, or
# when you run:  sudo greybox-ctl exec topgen.info topgen-boot reload-dns
#
# Format as in /etc/hosts: an IPv4 address, then one or more names. Any top
# level domain works, including made-up ones: the root and TLD servers get a
# zone for it, and every address gets a PTR record. Only A and PTR records.
# A name listed here wins over the same name from the scraped sites.
# These lines only add DNS records: the machine at the address must exist
# (e.g. a VM on the external 12.0.0.0/24 network).
#
#12.0.0.50    intranet.example.com example.com
#12.0.0.51    mail.foo.org
#12.0.0.52    portal.range.lab
